WEBVTT

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.960
<i>We continue to be met with much hardship.</i>

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.130
<i>We are strong as individuals,</i>

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.300
but as a pack,
our tribe is faced with grave danger.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.550
According to the human scientist
named Darwin,

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.180
it is not the strongest that survives,

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.510
but rather those that can adjust
to their circumstances.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.930
<i>Soon, this world will change immensely.</i>

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.020
<i>There is no need for us</i>
<i>to adjust to this world.</i>

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:00.360
<i>We are going to change</i>
<i>the shape of the world.</i>

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.780
It's almost time. Are you ready?

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.240
Let's make it a loud song.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.620
Maybe a peaceful one is better?

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:12.870
Yuliy, you're one to talk.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.170
Now it's only a matter of time.
Here's hoping for our blood to flourish,

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.800
and to celebrate
the beginning of a new world.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.260
Cheers!

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.330
-Hey, wait.
-I said wait!

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:55.870
Philip, it's time.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:58.460
Here you go.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.590
I can play this one better.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:03.630
Mr. Kershner.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:07.050
Oh... how inconvenient.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:10.430
If we're going to cross the ocean,
we have to mimic humans.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:15.680
Also... we have information that
the Jaegers have tracked us here.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.100
It's considered polite
to entertain guests.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.980
It may not be.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:26.150
Mr. Yevgraf's intentions to shed
unnecessary blood before an important job.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:30.700
Right. Well, considering how tough
the negotiations in Shanghai were...

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:33.490
I guess I'll leave this to you all.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.580
Those guys...
they tried to rip us off on our drinks.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:41.580
Next time you get into a fight,
invite me too.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.130
Jeez.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.050
Each of you, be cautious.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.840
We'll begin the performance as planned.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.350
Having a party with all those
expensive looking ladies, huh?

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.940
I hear Kershner is also here.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.610
Let's split up into two groups,
just as the professor has planned.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:06.900
<i>It's the smell of blood.</i>

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.220
-Yuliy!
-That idiot!

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.470
Now we have no choice!

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.830
It seems Kershner is not here.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.290
Yuliy!

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:03.670
Don't take off on your own!
Do you want to die?

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.920
I cleaned up nicely, didn't I?

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:10.420
You... Damn it!
You must have a death wish!

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:11.630
A death wish?

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.430
Maybe he doesn't value his life.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.730
You made a mess as usual.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:30.900
I'm sorry for acting selfishly.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.110
Yuliy.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.450
We cooperate as a "pack."

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.240
Each of us compensates
for what others may lack.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.450
And... we chase our prey endlessly,

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.870
corner them against the wall,
and kill them.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.540
That is our job.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:51.420
<i>I am a Jaeger.</i>

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:54.590
<i>And I...</i>

00:04:56.090 --> 00:05:00.010
EPISODE 1
THE REVENANT HOWLS IN DARKNESS

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:06.980
It's over here.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.450
-Hey, are you all right?
-What a gruesome murder.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.870
I thought this was
the Hyakko Party's doing,

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.330
but judging how the bodies were
mutilated, it must be Kuratake.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.010
We stand out a great deal.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.590
Really? These days,

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:41.810
I bet foreigners aren't that unusual.

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:44.470
Or is it my nice body
that makes us stand out?

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:45.730
You're right.

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:48.230
The way your flesh is
packed in tightly is quite...

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:50.270
Oh, excuse me.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.280
This country did used to

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.900
slay foreigners until a little while ago
in the name of exclusionism.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.570
That's horrifying.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.290
-Are you feeling nostalgic?
-No.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.910
This is my first time in this country.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.830
You must be from V Shipping!

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.540
I'm with the Naoe Family.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:15.380
Thank you for coming to pick us up.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:22.600
Everyone! The recent deterioration
of the Imperial Capital's public safety

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:23.760
cannot be overlooked...

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.970
That'll be 14 Sen.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.520
-Thanks.
-Thank you.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.190
Break it up, break it up!

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:31.560
...of the radical organization
Hyakko Party...

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:32.770
What are you doing?

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.070
Where do you think this is?

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.530
So noisy.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.650
They're just like bullies
picking on the weak.

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.320
By the way, Major Iba.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:44.120
The police seem certain
this morning's incident

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.040
was the work of the escaped prisoner.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:49.000
-Then it wasn't the Hyakko Party?
-No, sir.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.500
The messages they leave behind
weren't found at the scene.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:54.670
I'm also certain
it was the work of Kuratake.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.090
Mochizuki, you should avoid

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:59.220
making definitive statements
when you have so little information.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:00.800
-Yes, sir!
-Also...

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:04.220
could you not call me major
when I'm in my civilian clothes?

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:07.060
It may not seem so,
but I tend to mind my surroundings.

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:08.930
Yes, sir. I'm sorry, sir!

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:28.950
That'll be all.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:34.580
Miss Ryoko, you have improved yet again.

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:37.630
Then, Sensei,
how well will my sword-fighting skills

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:41.170
stand against the escaped prisoner
who is causing a stir among the public?

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:45.220
Miss, they say,
"A wise man keeps away from danger."

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.430
Being energetic is one thing but...

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:53.230
-What's that?
-Oh, they must be the Baron's guests.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:58.360
I hear they're an
international shipping company.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:02.900
When I was involved
with the last European Great War,

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:06.740
we were very grateful for all the help
we received from everyone at V Shipping.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:09.700
We would be happy
if we could return that favor now.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:11.290
Thank you.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.000
In any case,
you all speak Japanese so well.

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:18.170
Well, in our line of work,
there's an urgent need to.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.960
However, it's been a while visiting Japan

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.680
and it's as though
we've come to a different country.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:26.470
Indeed it is a different country.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.100
That's how tremendous the economical
and industrial growths have been.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.180
-However...
-Yes?

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:38.820
Those who now live in
the Imperial Capital all fear the night,

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:41.940
and live each day
without being able to relax.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:46.070
Could you tell me more
about that in detail?

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.490
Your rooms are in the annex,
further down this way.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:54.250
Hey, hey. Don't leave me behind.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:58.460
Jeez. Can't I go to the bathroom in peace?

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:00.840
Hey. Where's Yuliy?

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:05.550
He said he smelled
"the scent of flowers" just now.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:06.590
What?

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:31.410
Do you like flowers?

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:36.250
I'm Ryoko Naoe,
the daughter of this family.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:39.880
I'm...Yuliy.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:41.590
Yuliy...

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.550
That's a wonderful name.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:45.670
Do you like them?

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:48.970
We also raise many imported flowers here,

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:52.140
and even import fertilizers
and pesticides from abroad.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.810
This Western-style garden
is my father's pride.

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:58.730
-But you've spoiled them.
-Pardon?

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:02.610
They've been given
too much water and fertilizer.

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:04.190
They're rotting from the roots.

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:09.410
The anti-government organization
Hyakko Party.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:12.080
They claim that their purpose
is to bring back

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.290
the lost Samurai warrior spirit
and to offer salvation to the poor,

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:18.210
but in actuality,
they're thieves who target the rich.

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:22.250
And the escaped death row prisoner
Goichiro Kuratake...

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:26.010
This serial killer used to
only target young men.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:27.260
After his escape,

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.970
he has already proceeded
to cause multiple incidents.

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:34.310
Brutal incidents
occurring at the same time...

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:36.390
It can't be a coincidence.

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.600
-What?
-Oh, it's nothing.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.400
It's so sweet!

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:47.320
This is delicious, Dorothea.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:49.740
-I'll have it later.
-Oh, okay.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:53.620
This rich aroma.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:56.290
This rich aroma, it reminds me
of Ireland, my homeland.

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:00.120
It's hard to imagine a guy like you
being homesick.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:04.920
Anyhow, is Kershner
really here in this country?

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:06.630
We did lose him in Shanghai,

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:08.920
but V Shipping's intelligence is accurate.

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:10.050
Jeez.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:13.010
Why did he come all the way out here,
to the Far East?

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:14.890
To feast, perhaps?

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:17.850
All this trouble
for something that simple?

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:20.350
Well, it is an awful lot of time
and effort.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:25.360
Perhaps it can't be measured
by human common sense.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:28.360
They have a world of their own.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:33.110
The two worlds may collide,
but never will they come together.

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:37.040
Yuliy.

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.830
It sounds convincing when you say it.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:47.750
Going out for a stroll again?

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:49.170
Just like a doggy.

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:52.840
Struck a nerve, did I?

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:58.010
You two should get along better!
We're friends, right? We're friends.

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:00.850
Stop, don't touch my hair. Hey!

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:04.020
-Take this. You like this?
-Don't treat me like a child!

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:05.440
You're getting along well.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:08.900
-Does it seem that way, professor?
-I'm definitely going to

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:11.320
-get you for this...
-Be sure to rest well today.

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:13.400
We'll be busy from tomorrow.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:16.620
Yes... Then we'll talk again later.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:21.410
You do know about
this morning's incident, yes?

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:22.540
Yes, sir.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:24.040
Major Iba.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:28.290
Do you think the Hyakko Party had
something to do with Kuratake's escape?

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:30.710
I have obtained
the police's internal documents,

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.510
but that is an unlikely scenario.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:35.970
There are even questionable stories
about the Ministry of Interior

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:39.930
giving some strange foreigners permission
for their activities.

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:44.520
As the Military Bureau,
we cannot just stand by and watch.

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:48.150
That is why I think it's time for us,
the Kudan branch to take action.

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:51.030
If the Ministry of Interior
finds out about this,

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:53.530
it'll mean more than trouble.

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:57.950
After all,
our job is to rough up their turf.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:01.490
I demanded the impossible
of the Harbin Secret Military Agency

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:02.870
for your homeland return.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.920
-Do live up to that expectation.
-Yes, sir.

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:08.380
When can you start?

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:11.090
Already have.

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:29.940
I will come pick you up, Ms. Agatha,

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:32.480
-by the scheduled time.
-Please do.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:38.280
What on earth are you planning by
making me escape from prison?

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:40.200
Oh, are you frightened?

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:42.290
But you're a murderer!

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:44.830
Are you going to kill...?

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:46.290
Kill me?

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.380
You have an important role to play...

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:55.590
We know what Kuratake's face looks like!

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:58.260
Why hasn't he been caught
despite the emergency alert

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:01.260
put out in response
to all these killings? For all we know,

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:03.100
he's never worked with an accomplice.

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:04.180
Listen up!

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:07.520
We will double the number of
police officers on patrol from tonight!

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:09.730
Do not let him have his way any longer!

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:11.650
-Inspector!
-Shut up! What do you want?

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:14.030
Well, just now...

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:20.240
What!? V Shipping?

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:27.410
We have already been informed
by the Detective Sergeant, Mr. Willard.

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:30.670
The Ministry of Interior
also strongly requested

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:32.840
that we fully cooperate with you.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:34.420
Thank you.

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:37.090
We will take a look then.

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:38.550
Yes, yes.

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:42.180
By the way,
what is your exact role in this...?

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:44.220
Let's just say you can think of us

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:47.350
as heroes of justice
from across the ocean.

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:55.780
So, how many more houses to check?

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:30.560
Before the arrest,
Kuratake only targeted young men.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:32.730
But after the prison escape,

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:35.650
he has been targeting people of any age,
man or woman.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.280
His tendencies have clearly changed.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:41.780
The police seem to think
that he is acting indiscriminately

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:43.160
because he is on the run.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.280
But is that really the reason?

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:48.950
Is it all right to show those
suspicious foreigners

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:50.370
the investigation documents?

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:53.080
Orders from above.
There's nothing we can do.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:56.880
Inspector! There was a murder at Akasaka!

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:57.840
What?

00:15:58.050 --> 00:16:00.630
-It can't be him again, can it?
-Let's join the others.

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:10.310
From reading the documents,

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:12.310
it seems the Hyakko Party

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:15.310
is unrelated to the prison break
and the following incidents.

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.110
Anything on the prison?

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:20.190
Escaping that prison
is difficult without any help.

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:23.820
But there's no record of him
ever working with accomplices.

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:26.660
However, a person's shadow
that seemed to be

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:28.780
jumping around the area
has been witnessed.

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:31.620
But it seems this was
a mistaken witness report

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:32.620
made by a drunk.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.250
Security patrols have been tightened,

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:37.670
but despite that,
this killer has not been caught.

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:40.590
It's because
they're chasing after Kuratake.

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:46.220
<i>He did not commit the murder?</i>

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:49.220
I doubt he is even alive.

00:16:49.890 --> 00:16:54.060
Then, who let Kuratake escape
to make it look like he did it?

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:56.810
It's them...

00:16:58.610 --> 00:16:59.940
<i>our prey.</i>

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:34.930
The police...

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:37.650
What?

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:43.320
The police are too caught up
with finding that man, Kuratake.

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:46.650
On top of that,
they would never suspect a woman.

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:51.370
What are you talking about?
I haven't the faintest idea.

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:54.160
-Oh, but I can smell it.
-What?

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:56.460
I can smell it coming from your body.

00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:00.080
It's that smell of rusty iron
and rotten fish.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.210
The smell of blood!

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:10.340
It's the vampire smell!
The one that makes me want to vomit!

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:12.430
-A Jaeger?
-Hey!

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:14.390
What are you doing over there?

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:24.360
Hey! Stop!

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:34.580
He doesn't look tasty, that old man.

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:40.500
Good job.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:49.300
Jaegers! They've come chasing us
all the way here!

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:07.190
Fallon, make sure to follow them!

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:08.360
Leave it to me!

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:38.140
Yuliy? Don't be reckless,

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:40.810
-this isn't a circus!
-Can you get closer to their car?

00:19:41.310 --> 00:19:42.560
That's what I'm doing!

00:19:57.660 --> 00:20:00.330
-Damn it! Hurry up and go, Fallon!
-Give me a minute!

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:50.920
You dirty Jaeger!

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:09.060
It can't be. You're Sirius.

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:25.580
The Royals...

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:28.420
Yuliy!

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:31.550
Don't pursue this any further. Yuliy!

00:21:56.950 --> 00:21:58.110
Yuliy!

00:23:31.460 --> 00:23:32.290
Enter.

00:23:36.590 --> 00:23:38.340
The Jaegers are in Japan?

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:41.260
Yes. Agatha was hurt.

00:23:43.010 --> 00:23:44.720
As expected.

00:23:45.220 --> 00:23:46.470
They have a keen nose.

00:23:55.940 --> 00:23:57.900
<i>-It's too late.</i>
<i>-Are you Mr. Willard?</i>

00:23:57.980 --> 00:23:59.400
<i>The Royals the other day...</i>

00:23:59.490 --> 00:24:01.860
<i>Almost there, almost there, Saki.</i>

00:24:01.950 --> 00:24:03.700
<i>-Artificial heart...</i>
<i>-You Sirius scum!</i>

00:24:03.780 --> 00:24:04.950
EPISODE 2
DEPRIVED TALENT

00:24:14.580 --> 00:24:17.960
Subtitle translation by Haruna Saito
